        { "gurmukhi": "ਤੁਸੀਂ", "romanised": "tusi", "meaning": "you (polite)", "grammarNote": "subject" },
        { "gurmukhi": "ਕਿਵੇਂ", "romanised": "kiven", "meaning": "how", "grammarNote": "question word" },
        { "gurmukhi": "ਹੋ", "romanised": "ho", "meaning": "are", "grammarNote": "verb — always comes last" }
      ],
      "note": "Notice that Punjabi puts the verb at the end of the sentence — literally \"you how are?\""
